# linux/scripts/03-media/core/arch-flags-amd64.env
#
# Per-target-arch media build skip flags for amd64 (native full-feature
# builds, and the default when no cross build is active).
# Loaded by media_load_arch_flags() in 03-media/core/common.sh.
# Format: KEY=value lines only (shell-safe; the file is sourced by bash).
# 1 = skip, 0/unset = do not skip.
#
# amd64 is the native full-feature configuration: nothing is skipped, so this
# file intentionally sets no MEDIA_SKIP_* flags. Every consumer reads them as
# "${MEDIA_SKIP_*:-0}", i.e. unset already means "do not skip" — the explicit
# =0 lines this file used to carry were redundant. It is kept as a comment-only
# stub (rather than deleted) only because linux/Dockerfile.media COPYs it by
# name into the media base stage; media_load_arch_flags() itself already
# tolerates the file's absence.
